WEBVTT

00:00:07.130 --> 00:00:09.960
"JULY 9, 2095"

00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:11.050
"1- MIYUKI SHIBA"
"2- HONOKA MITSUI"
"3- SHIZUKU KITAYAMA"
"4- HAGANE TOMITSUKA"

00:00:11.050 --> 00:00:12.760
Yay!

00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:15.680
Well, the results
are just as expected, huh?

00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:17.640
Congratulations to you, too, Miyuki!

00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:19.470
There's my name right next to my brother's!

00:00:19.470 --> 00:00:21.220
"1- TATSUYA SHIBA"
"2- MIYUKI SHIBA"

00:00:19.470 --> 00:00:21.220
There's my name right next to my brother's!

00:00:23.310 --> 00:00:26.690
That's the one thing about you
that disappoints me, Miyuki.

00:00:26.690 --> 00:00:29.650
Or maybe you mean it's adorable!

00:00:29.650 --> 00:00:34.400
But these scores should get all three of us
picked for the Nine Schools Competition!

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:38.910
Yeah. That's why I crammed
like crazy to make it.

00:00:38.910 --> 00:00:41.120
I want to get chosen, no matter what!

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:44.660
Shizuku, you're on fire. What's going on?

00:00:44.660 --> 00:00:49.040
Oh, the Nine Schools Competition
always sends Shizuku into beast mode.

00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:51.420
Every year, she goes alone to watch...

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:54.420
to gather data on all the frontrunners.

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:59.010
Oh my! So, this year, you won't be
a spectator but a contestant!

00:00:59.010 --> 00:01:01.510
Yeah. I hope it turns out that way.

00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:03.560
"STUDENT COUNCIL OFFICE"

00:01:03.560 --> 00:01:06.690
No official announcements yet on our lineup,

00:01:06.690 --> 00:01:09.980
but this year's class of rookies is so deep,
we can really depend on them!

00:01:09.980 --> 00:01:13.820
Mitsui and Kitayama
are sure to be picked, too.

00:01:14.940 --> 00:01:15.610
"NINE SCHOOLS COMPETITION"

00:01:15.610 --> 00:01:19.280
"NINE SCHOOLS COMPETITION"

00:01:15.610 --> 00:01:19.280
The National Magic High School
Goodwill Tournament of Magic Skills...

00:01:19.280 --> 00:01:22.160
Also known as the "Nine Schools Competition."

00:01:22.160 --> 00:01:26.500
Every year, the cream of the crop
of magic high school students gather

00:01:26.500 --> 00:01:29.500
to compete against each other
on this dazzling stage.

00:01:29.500 --> 00:01:33.960
I'm expecting great things of you
as a valuable asset to our team!

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:35.420
I'm counting on you!

00:01:35.420 --> 00:01:36.550
Okay!

00:03:12.190 --> 00:03:14.360
"JULY 18, 2095"
"NINE SCHOOLS COMPETITION
DAY OF INAUGURATION"

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:16.400
I'm Shiba from Class 1-E.

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:19.650
During the Nine Schools Competition,
I'll be adjusting your CADs,

00:03:19.650 --> 00:03:23.950
creating your training regimens
and formulating strategies for you.

00:03:23.950 --> 00:03:27.450
He's a member of the technical staff
that will support you!

00:03:27.450 --> 00:03:31.410
Ask him anything! Don't hold back!

00:03:31.410 --> 00:03:33.830
So, we're getting a guy.

00:03:33.830 --> 00:03:37.300
I would've preferred a female engineer.

00:03:37.300 --> 00:03:39.800
--Um...
--Uh...

00:03:39.800 --> 00:03:41.590
About that, see--

00:03:41.590 --> 00:03:46.010
I thought that would be better myself, but...

00:03:46.010 --> 00:03:50.390
We don't need
any Course 2 student's support!

00:03:50.390 --> 00:03:51.770
The thing is...

00:03:51.770 --> 00:03:54.810
I got turned down by the guys first.

00:03:54.810 --> 00:03:57.610
Seriously, how stupid can guys be?

00:03:57.610 --> 00:04:01.110
You'd think the test scores
would give them an idea!

00:04:01.110 --> 00:04:06.240
A Course 2 student being named to the tech
staff is already unprecedented enough.

00:04:06.240 --> 00:04:10.330
There's no greater proof
that Tatsuya is that talented.

00:04:10.330 --> 00:04:16.330
Right! How lucky are we to get the support
of someone like that? Right, Miyuki?

00:04:16.330 --> 00:04:17.420
Right!

00:04:17.420 --> 00:04:20.130
Whether you're a guy
or a Course 2 student,

00:04:20.130 --> 00:04:23.760
as long as you're exceptional
at your job, what do I care?

00:04:23.760 --> 00:04:26.590
If you say so, Subaru.

00:04:26.590 --> 00:04:28.300
I'm looking forward
to working with you!

00:04:28.300 --> 00:04:33.100
Tatsuya, I want to talk to you about the magic
I'll be using in Ice Pillars Break--

00:04:33.100 --> 00:04:35.100
Hey, no fair, Shizuku!

00:04:35.100 --> 00:04:37.810
I'd like you to adjust my CAD, too!

00:04:37.810 --> 00:04:39.230
Mine, too, then!

00:04:39.230 --> 00:04:41.780
Mine, too! Please!

00:04:46.450 --> 00:04:50.410
Brother, you seemed to be
enjoying yourself a lot this afternoon.

00:04:50.410 --> 00:04:52.750
Did I? I'll admit...

00:04:52.750 --> 00:04:58.630
that talking to the brilliant magicians chosen
for the Nine Schools Competition was intriguing.

00:04:58.630 --> 00:05:00.050
I knew it!

00:05:01.210 --> 00:05:04.130
Honoka, Shizuku, Eimi,
Subaru and the others...

00:05:04.130 --> 00:05:07.340
They're all so sweet and lovely, aren't they?

00:05:08.800 --> 00:05:10.430
Hello? Ms. Miyuki?

00:05:10.430 --> 00:05:12.520
Don't you think you're misreading
something here?

00:05:12.520 --> 00:05:15.770
Brother, for having such lecherous
thoughts while being surrounded

00:05:15.770 --> 00:05:17.940
by such lovely classmates...

00:05:19.770 --> 00:05:21.520
this is your punishment!

00:05:24.820 --> 00:05:27.030
Self-Repair Spell.

00:05:27.030 --> 00:05:31.330
Reading the Eidos from a backup
and restoring it.

00:05:31.330 --> 00:05:34.410
This is my brother's specialty magic.

00:05:34.410 --> 00:05:39.250
So, this is no more than roughhousing
between two siblings.

00:05:39.250 --> 00:05:42.050
No matter how drastic
their measures may be,

00:05:42.050 --> 00:05:46.970
no one can ever hurt my brother, after all.

00:05:51.350 --> 00:05:53.220
Please forgive me.

00:05:53.220 --> 00:05:56.140
I went too far with my prank.

00:05:56.140 --> 00:05:58.440
Give me a break, will you?

00:06:05.990 --> 00:06:08.030
"AUGUST 1, 2095"

00:06:08.030 --> 00:06:10.320
"AUGUST 1, 2095"
"2095 NATIONAL MAGIC HIGH SCHOOL
GOODWILL TOURNAMENT OF MAGIC SKILLS"

00:06:10.450 --> 00:06:12.780
"SAME DAY"
"ATHLETES' VILLAGE"
"SOCIAL GATHERING VENUE"

00:06:19.420 --> 00:06:24.300
Here they are! The favorites to win and
the most powerful team of all, Third High!

00:06:24.300 --> 00:06:26.720
That's the Crimson Prince, right?

00:06:26.720 --> 00:06:29.130
The prince of the Ichijo Family
of the Ten Master Clans!

00:06:29.130 --> 00:06:31.680
And with him is Cardinal Joji!

00:06:31.680 --> 00:06:34.260
They're Third High's golden combo!

00:06:35.850 --> 00:06:37.390
Seriously...

00:06:37.390 --> 00:06:41.230
How carefree they are
on the eve of battle!

00:06:41.230 --> 00:06:45.570
You'd think they were mistaking
this get-together for something else.

00:06:45.570 --> 00:06:49.070
It only goes to show you
how many people have their guard down.

00:06:49.070 --> 00:06:51.910
I'm calling it,
Third High's going to breeze to victory!

00:06:51.910 --> 00:06:55.580
Toko, you shouldn't be so cavalier about it.

00:06:56.750 --> 00:06:58.040
Huh?

00:07:03.040 --> 00:07:05.050
--So, that's First High.
--Ms. Mari!

00:07:05.050 --> 00:07:07.710
The almighty generation bidding
for their third straight victory.

00:07:07.710 --> 00:07:11.340
I hear they were involved
in a traffic accident on their way here,

00:07:11.340 --> 00:07:13.220
but it looks like they made it out okay, huh?

00:07:13.220 --> 00:07:14.680
I'm glad that they did.

00:07:14.680 --> 00:07:16.850
There's no better way to prove our abilities

00:07:16.850 --> 00:07:19.390
than by defeating our
opponents in top condition.

00:07:19.390 --> 00:07:21.390
M-Mr. Ichijo?

00:07:21.390 --> 00:07:23.400
What's the matter?

00:07:26.070 --> 00:07:28.070
So beautiful.

00:07:28.070 --> 00:07:30.240
Ichijo?

00:07:30.240 --> 00:07:33.450
Who on earth could he be
so mesmerized by?

00:07:44.580 --> 00:07:46.170
Who is that girl?

00:07:46.170 --> 00:07:49.050
I don't blame Ichijo
for not being able to take his eyes off her.

00:07:49.050 --> 00:07:52.180
Even I nearly had a heart attack.

00:07:54.720 --> 00:07:59.720
I can see that you must be
from an illustrious family.

00:07:59.720 --> 00:08:03.730
I'm Airi Isshiki,
a first year at Third High School.

00:08:03.730 --> 00:08:05.560
As is Shiori Kanou...

00:08:05.560 --> 00:08:08.270
and Toko Tsukushiin here.

00:08:08.270 --> 00:08:12.150
I'm Miyuki Shiba,
a first year at First High School.

00:08:12.150 --> 00:08:13.450
"Shiba"?

00:08:13.450 --> 00:08:15.820
That doesn't sound familiar.

00:08:15.820 --> 00:08:18.740
Ms. Mizuo, it's underway already, isn't it?

00:08:18.740 --> 00:08:21.790
The rivalry at the get-together before battle!

00:08:21.790 --> 00:08:25.210
Yes. That's the appeal
of the Nine Schools Competition!

00:08:25.210 --> 00:08:29.340
Well, in our day,
First High was so overwhelmingly strong,

00:08:29.340 --> 00:08:33.050
we were too intimidated
to go up to them and say hello.

00:08:33.050 --> 00:08:35.010
Really, now!

00:08:35.010 --> 00:08:37.100
How obnoxious was that?

00:08:37.100 --> 00:08:38.600
What's that girl's problem?

00:08:38.600 --> 00:08:42.310
Oh dear, so you're just members
of the rank and file, then?

00:08:42.310 --> 00:08:46.520
I only spoke to you because I was sure
you were of illustrious lineage.

00:08:46.520 --> 00:08:48.650
Please forgive my mistake!

00:08:48.650 --> 00:08:51.990
Good luck to you in your events!

00:08:51.990 --> 00:08:55.660
What did she mean by that?
Like she even has a clue!

00:08:55.660 --> 00:08:58.320
If she only knew
how incredible Miyuki is! Really!

00:08:58.320 --> 00:09:02.950
Airi Isshiki. Also known as Éclair Airi.

00:09:02.950 --> 00:09:06.420
A daughter of one
of the 18 Assistant Houses, the Isshikis,

00:09:06.420 --> 00:09:09.210
who, thanks to her piercing
Movement Spell attacks,

00:09:09.210 --> 00:09:13.210
came to be known as
"Éclair" or "Lightning."

00:09:13.210 --> 00:09:15.340
What? She's only a first year,

00:09:15.340 --> 00:09:17.840
and she's going to compete
in the Official Mirage Bat Event?

00:09:17.840 --> 00:09:20.310
Brushing aside the upperclassmen?

00:09:20.310 --> 00:09:23.390
Those two she was with
are also first years...

00:09:23.390 --> 00:09:25.600
and both are players to beat.

00:09:25.600 --> 00:09:29.020
I'm sure we'll be facing off
with them in the Rookie Events.

00:09:29.020 --> 00:09:30.770
Okay!

00:09:30.770 --> 00:09:33.570
Now it's really weighing heavy on my mind!

00:09:36.490 --> 00:09:38.740
Eimi? What's up?

00:09:39.620 --> 00:09:41.660
We're going to the hot spring!

00:09:44.080 --> 00:09:46.080
This feels so good!

00:09:46.080 --> 00:09:48.960
Who knew there was a place like this?

00:09:48.960 --> 00:09:50.750
But really, Honoka...

00:09:50.750 --> 00:09:52.630
You sure are well-developed!

00:09:52.630 --> 00:09:54.090
Huh?

00:09:54.090 --> 00:09:56.720
Would you mind if I peeled them?

00:09:56.720 --> 00:09:58.840
Of course I mind!

00:09:58.840 --> 00:10:01.010
Then let me massage them!

00:10:01.010 --> 00:10:03.720
What do you mean by "then"?

00:10:05.810 --> 00:10:10.690
This is when you either peel them
or massage them! I saw it on an anime show!

00:10:10.690 --> 00:10:13.110
You watch too much weird anime!

00:10:13.110 --> 00:10:15.440
Rescue me, Shizuku!

00:10:15.440 --> 00:10:20.320
You'll be fine, since you at least
have something to massage.

00:10:20.320 --> 00:10:22.410
Now that we have permission...

00:10:25.660 --> 00:10:28.500
What in the world is this commotion about?

00:10:30.830 --> 00:10:35.590
You shouldn't make so much noise,
or you'll end up annoying the other guests.

00:10:48.940 --> 00:10:52.310
Wh-What's the matter?

00:10:52.310 --> 00:10:53.940
I don't know.

00:10:53.940 --> 00:10:56.900
It's like another door is about to open!

00:10:58.820 --> 00:11:01.700
Oh boy, what a close call!

00:11:01.700 --> 00:11:04.280
The allure of Miyuki's pale skin!

00:11:04.280 --> 00:11:07.910
I don't want to think about what could've
happened if you hadn't snapped out of it!

00:11:07.910 --> 00:11:10.330
Anyway, you were way out of line, Eimi!

00:11:10.330 --> 00:11:14.840
But your breasts were so springy,
it felt amazing!

00:11:14.840 --> 00:11:16.380
"Springy"...

00:11:16.380 --> 00:11:18.470
Lucky you.

00:11:18.470 --> 00:11:19.920
That's...

00:11:19.920 --> 00:11:22.800
The First High students
we met at the get-together.

00:11:22.800 --> 00:11:27.270
A conversation about someone's breasts...
How vulgar is that?

00:11:27.270 --> 00:11:32.900
Well, not that you'd have any interest in that,
Airi, but it's so... I don't know... Ordinary.

00:11:32.900 --> 00:11:35.230
Hey! What do you mean by that?

00:11:35.230 --> 00:11:36.940
Anyway...

00:11:36.940 --> 00:11:39.650
rather than worry about those frivolous fools,

00:11:39.650 --> 00:11:42.200
we just need to do what we have to do.

00:11:42.200 --> 00:11:46.790
We'll be the ones
to build Third High's new future!

00:11:53.250 --> 00:11:53.500
"AUGUST 3, 2095"

00:11:53.500 --> 00:11:56.040
"AUGUST 3, 2095"

00:11:53.500 --> 00:11:56.040
At last, it is time to open the National Magic
High School Goodwill Tournament of Magic Skills,

00:11:56.040 --> 00:11:57.550
At last, it is time to open the National Magic
High School Goodwill Tournament of Magic Skills,

00:11:57.550 --> 00:12:00.510
the Nine Schools Competition!

00:12:00.510 --> 00:12:02.880
Over the next ten days of furious competition...

00:12:02.880 --> 00:12:04.890
the Official Events
with no grade restrictions,

00:12:04.890 --> 00:12:09.390
and the Rookie Events limited to
first years will serve as battlegrounds!

00:12:09.390 --> 00:12:10.770
Now...

00:12:10.770 --> 00:12:13.770
which high school will be
the one to grasp all the glory?

00:12:14.230 --> 00:12:15.110
"FIRST HIGH SCHOOL"

00:12:15.110 --> 00:12:18.440
"FIRST HIGH SCHOOL"

00:12:15.110 --> 00:12:18.440
So, just as we suspected,
that bus accident yesterday was...

00:12:18.440 --> 00:12:21.360
There were multiple traces of magic.

00:12:21.360 --> 00:12:26.280
There's no question that it was sabotage
under the guise of an accident.

00:12:26.280 --> 00:12:29.160
But don't you worry.

00:12:29.160 --> 00:12:31.660
I'll protect you, no matter what, Miyuki.

00:12:31.660 --> 00:12:35.460
So, I want you to relax
and focus on your events.

00:12:35.460 --> 00:12:37.380
Brother!

00:12:37.380 --> 00:12:40.460
This is your biggest moment as a student.

00:12:40.460 --> 00:12:42.130
Let me see it, too.

00:12:42.880 --> 00:12:45.180
Right. I'll do that.

00:12:45.840 --> 00:12:46.970
"KEIKO MATOBA (FIFTH HIGH SCHOOL)"

00:12:45.840 --> 00:12:46.970
"MAYUMI SAEGUSA (FIRST HIGH SCHOOL)"

00:12:46.970 --> 00:12:49.810
"KEIKO MATOBA (FIFTH HIGH SCHOOL)"
"MAYUMI SAEGUSA (FIRST HIGH SCHOOL)"

00:12:46.970 --> 00:12:49.810
The first event is Speed Shooting!

00:12:49.810 --> 00:12:54.600
Using magic to destroy the launched targets,
you vie to hit more than anyone else!

00:13:10.160 --> 00:13:12.000
Wow! Perfect!

00:13:12.000 --> 00:13:14.540
Winner, First High's Elfin Sniper...

00:13:14.540 --> 00:13:16.750
Mayumi Saegusa!

00:13:16.750 --> 00:13:19.670
--Her third straight victory!
--Ms. Mayumi! You're so amazing!

00:13:20.050 --> 00:13:21.550
"BATTLE BOARD"

00:13:21.550 --> 00:13:22.590
Next...

00:13:22.590 --> 00:13:25.220
Women's Battle Board trials!

00:13:25.220 --> 00:13:26.970
Navigating a 3 km water route,

00:13:26.970 --> 00:13:30.640
the players will draw upon Acceleration Magic
to compete for supremacy!

00:13:30.640 --> 00:13:34.480
Look at that!
Back as the frontrunner again this year,

00:13:34.480 --> 00:13:38.690
First High's Mari Watanabe
is running away with the race!

00:13:39.940 --> 00:13:41.570
We love you!

00:13:41.570 --> 00:13:42.900
Ms. Mari!

00:13:42.900 --> 00:13:44.280
Hug me!

00:13:44.280 --> 00:13:45.990
Listen to that crowd!

00:13:45.990 --> 00:13:50.330
It seems like our upperclasswomen
have some enthusiastic fans!

00:13:50.330 --> 00:13:55.410
They say that Ms. Watanabe
is a lock to win the Mirage Bat Event, too.

00:13:55.410 --> 00:13:58.420
No wonder the almighty generation
has a two-year winning streak.

00:13:59.920 --> 00:14:05.050
I bet that Miyuki will be famous
after this competition, too.

00:14:11.680 --> 00:14:12.970
"AUGUST 5, 2095"

00:14:15.730 --> 00:14:18.690
Miyuki's overall abilities are overwhelming,

00:14:18.690 --> 00:14:22.320
and Shizuku can brute-force
her way through magic spells.

00:14:22.320 --> 00:14:26.110
If I'm going to catch up to them,
I'll have to train twice as hard!

00:14:26.950 --> 00:14:29.740
Honoka!

00:14:29.740 --> 00:14:31.410
Tatsuya?

00:14:33.030 --> 00:14:36.710
I see you're starting really early to train.

00:14:40.040 --> 00:14:42.540
S-Sorry...

00:14:42.540 --> 00:14:44.920
to make you help me out.

00:14:45.880 --> 00:14:47.760
Don't worry about it.

00:14:47.760 --> 00:14:49.630
But I'm impressed.

00:14:49.630 --> 00:14:54.430
You're not dialing down your training
even in the middle of the competition.

00:14:54.430 --> 00:14:58.770
Well, I feel as though I'll get rusty
if I take off even one day.

00:14:59.690 --> 00:15:01.980
That's the right mindset to have.

00:15:01.980 --> 00:15:05.820
The events you're competing in...
Battle Board and Mirage Bat...

00:15:05.820 --> 00:15:10.910
call for physical balance control
as much as magic power.

00:15:10.910 --> 00:15:15.740
It's important that you keep this up to maintain
your current condition for your Rookie Events.

00:15:15.740 --> 00:15:17.540
R-Right!

00:15:20.080 --> 00:15:22.210
His face is so close!

00:15:23.170 --> 00:15:25.500
Wh-Wh-What am I going to do?

00:15:25.500 --> 00:15:28.800
Tatsuya's going to hear my heart pounding!

00:15:28.800 --> 00:15:31.470
Give it all you've got, Honoka.

00:15:31.470 --> 00:15:34.260
Give it all you've got, Honoka.

00:15:34.260 --> 00:15:36.560
Honoka...

00:15:36.560 --> 00:15:38.390
R-Right!

00:15:38.390 --> 00:15:39.980
I'll give it all I've got!

00:15:40.350 --> 00:15:41.350
"THIRD HIGH SCHOOL"

00:15:41.350 --> 00:15:45.360
"THIRD HIGH SCHOOL"

00:15:41.350 --> 00:15:45.360
Ms. Mizuo! Good luck
in the Battle Board semifinals!

00:15:45.360 --> 00:15:47.150
We're rooting for you!

00:15:47.150 --> 00:15:48.530
Thanks.

00:15:48.530 --> 00:15:53.240
I'm with First High's Watanabe and Seventh High
of the Seas. What a ridiculous group.

00:15:53.240 --> 00:15:55.410
Hey, but I'll just give it my best shot!

00:15:55.410 --> 00:16:00.540
But you can practically feel the tournament
committee's malice oozing from this matchup!

00:16:00.540 --> 00:16:04.670
If only First High, at least, had withdrawn
because of that bus accident.

00:16:04.670 --> 00:16:06.250
Um...

00:16:06.250 --> 00:16:08.550
You two!

00:16:08.550 --> 00:16:13.090
I won't tolerate you wishing misfortune
on other people, even in jest.

00:16:13.090 --> 00:16:17.600
For us magicians,
our image is reality itself.

00:16:18.890 --> 00:16:20.930
S-Sorry.

00:16:20.930 --> 00:16:25.150
Your opponents may be formidable,
but I know you can do it, Ms. Mizuo.

00:16:25.150 --> 00:16:26.650
I wish you the best of luck.

00:16:28.730 --> 00:16:31.780
Ms. Watanabe, going head-to-head
with Seventh High !

00:16:31.780 --> 00:16:33.610
Isn't this the same matchup
as last year's final?

00:16:33.610 --> 00:16:35.030
On your marks!

00:16:51.760 --> 00:16:55.390
Over-acceleration?
An easy mistake like that?

00:16:55.390 --> 00:16:56.510
Why?

00:16:56.510 --> 00:16:58.050
Stop!

00:17:04.480 --> 00:17:05.730
Look out!

00:17:17.280 --> 00:17:18.990
Ms. Watanabe!

00:17:19.080 --> 00:17:20.410
"SUSONO BASE HOSPITAL"

00:17:20.410 --> 00:17:25.040
"SUSONO BASE HOSPITAL"
They said you can resume
your normal life after a day, but...

00:17:25.040 --> 00:17:27.710
No activity for a week, huh?

00:17:27.710 --> 00:17:29.090
Sorry.

00:17:29.090 --> 00:17:30.630
Don't talk like that.

00:17:30.630 --> 00:17:34.840
Thank goodness neither you nor the
Seventh High student were seriously hurt.

00:17:34.840 --> 00:17:40.970
But now, we're no longer a lock
to win the official Mirage Bat Event.

00:17:40.970 --> 00:17:42.270
Right.

00:17:42.270 --> 00:17:46.100
As of now, it's still ours to lose.

00:17:46.100 --> 00:17:49.150
But we'll probably have to change our strategy.

00:17:49.980 --> 00:17:50.270
"SUSONO BASE HOSPITAL"

00:17:50.270 --> 00:17:53.490
"SUSONO BASE HOSPITAL"

00:17:50.270 --> 00:17:53.490
Thank goodness Ms. Watanabe
wasn't seriously injured!

00:17:53.490 --> 00:17:54.570
Thank goodness Ms. Watanabe
wasn't seriously injured!

00:17:54.570 --> 00:17:56.280
Y-Yeah.

00:17:56.280 --> 00:17:59.370
Really... I'm so glad.

00:17:59.370 --> 00:18:01.410
Are you all right, Honoka?

00:18:01.410 --> 00:18:04.540
Oh sure, I'm fine!

00:18:04.540 --> 00:18:07.960
--Let's head back!
--Okay.

00:18:07.960 --> 00:18:10.000
It's probably the Rookie Event.

00:18:10.000 --> 00:18:11.340
Right.

00:18:11.340 --> 00:18:14.170
Since Honoka's taking part
in Battle Board, too...

00:18:14.170 --> 00:18:16.680
I don't blame her for being anxious.

00:18:18.300 --> 00:18:23.060
By the way, Shiba's looking
into Watanabe's accident, right?

00:18:23.060 --> 00:18:29.650
Yes. Normally, Mari wouldn't have any
trouble riding out an accident of that level.

00:18:29.650 --> 00:18:31.480
Something must've happened.

00:18:31.480 --> 00:18:32.690
Interference?

00:18:32.690 --> 00:18:34.360
Most likely.

00:18:34.360 --> 00:18:39.110
The moment it happened, some kind of spell
was cast on the water's surface.

00:18:39.110 --> 00:18:42.740
Who knew we'd have to worry about
something other than the actual matches?

00:18:43.620 --> 00:18:45.290
"AUGUST 5, 2095"

00:18:43.620 --> 00:18:45.290
"END OF DAY 3"

00:18:45.290 --> 00:18:47.500
"AUGUST 5, 2095"
"END OF DAY 3"

00:18:45.290 --> 00:18:47.500
Ms. Chiyoda won the Women's
Ice Pillars Break Official Match.

00:18:47.500 --> 00:18:50.080
"IN USE"
"FIRST HIGH"

00:18:47.500 --> 00:18:50.080
Ms. Chiyoda won the Women's
Ice Pillars Break Official Match.

00:18:50.080 --> 00:18:52.500
With the end of the first half
of the Nine Schools Competition,

00:18:52.500 --> 00:18:56.170
the Rookie Events
will be starting tomorrow.

00:18:56.170 --> 00:18:59.130
Here are the overall scores as of today.

00:18:59.130 --> 00:19:01.850
Since Third High has been making
greater gains than we'd anticipated,

00:19:01.850 --> 00:19:03.600
our lead is now razor-thin.

00:19:03.600 --> 00:19:06.640
The only Official Events in the second half

00:19:06.640 --> 00:19:09.690
are the Women's Mirage Bat
and the Men's Monolith Code, right?

00:19:09.690 --> 00:19:11.020
Correct.

00:19:11.020 --> 00:19:17.190
Meaning that depending on our scores in the
Rookie Events, we could very well be overtaken.

00:19:17.190 --> 00:19:20.490
My bad. If I hadn't been so pathetic...

00:19:20.490 --> 00:19:23.200
That accident wasn't your fault,
Ms. Watanabe.

00:19:23.200 --> 00:19:27.580
And actually, we'd really rather
you stayed in bed, Ms. Watanabe.

00:19:27.580 --> 00:19:30.250
Don't treat me like an invalid!

00:19:30.250 --> 00:19:33.670
But this means we're going to need
a comeback strategy,

00:19:33.670 --> 00:19:37.340
thanks to my withdrawal
from Mirage Bat, right?

00:19:37.340 --> 00:19:39.130
So, we're going to focus
on the Official Events,

00:19:39.130 --> 00:19:42.930
even if it's somewhat
at the expense of the Rookie Events.

00:19:42.930 --> 00:19:45.140
That's the conclusion we've reached.

00:19:45.140 --> 00:19:50.020
Miyuki, we're going to have you take
Mari's place in the Official Mirage Bat Event

00:19:50.020 --> 00:19:52.190
rather than the Rookie Event.

00:19:54.730 --> 00:19:59.110
Ms. Mizuo!
Congratulations on winning Battle Board!

00:19:59.110 --> 00:20:02.320
--Congrats, Mizuo!
--You rock, Ms. Mizuo!

00:20:02.320 --> 00:20:04.200
Thank you so much!

00:20:07.830 --> 00:20:11.080
You don't look very happy.

00:20:11.080 --> 00:20:14.920
I may have won, but a win after all that...

00:20:14.920 --> 00:20:18.590
To be honest,
I can't feel truly happy about it.

00:20:18.590 --> 00:20:21.010
And now, this just in...

00:20:21.010 --> 00:20:26.260
In place of Mari Watanabe, who withdrew
after being involved in an accident,

00:20:26.260 --> 00:20:28.850
First High has submitted
the name of first year Miyuki Shiba...

00:20:28.850 --> 00:20:31.230
as her substitute
in the Official Mirage Bat Event.

00:20:31.230 --> 00:20:35.230
She was chosen from among the first years,
just like Ms. Isshiki?

00:20:35.230 --> 00:20:37.360
I wonder what kind of player she is.

00:20:37.360 --> 00:20:39.400
Masaki...

00:20:39.400 --> 00:20:40.940
Angel...

00:20:40.940 --> 00:20:42.610
Masaki?

00:20:42.610 --> 00:20:43.990
That's...

00:20:43.990 --> 00:20:45.780
...the girl from the get-together.

00:20:45.780 --> 00:20:47.530
Oh, you mean that one?

00:20:47.530 --> 00:20:50.250
So, she wasn't just anyone, after all.

00:20:50.250 --> 00:20:54.540
Airi, make sure you defeat her
and win, no matter what!

00:20:54.540 --> 00:20:58.460
I mean I'm not saying that
because she's Watanabe's replacement.

00:20:58.460 --> 00:21:00.590
I want you to beat that girl...

00:21:00.590 --> 00:21:03.260
to show everyone how powerful you are.

00:21:03.260 --> 00:21:06.760
I'll do everything in my power
to support you in that.

00:21:06.760 --> 00:21:10.180
Because you're the pride
of Third High, Airi Isshiki!

00:21:10.180 --> 00:21:11.890
Ms. Mizuo...

00:21:13.770 --> 00:21:15.560
It's not your support that I want.

00:21:15.560 --> 00:21:19.480
I want to achieve victory
with you, Ms. Mizuo!

00:21:19.480 --> 00:21:24.740
Let's go for a one-two finish for Third High
in the Official Mirage Bat Event!

00:21:25.740 --> 00:21:26.740
"NATIONAL MAGIC HIGH SCHOOL"

00:21:26.740 --> 00:21:29.620
"NATIONAL MAGIC HIGH SCHOOL"
"AUGUST 6, 2095"
"NINE SCHOOLS COMPETITION"
"DAY 4 OF THE GAMES FOR FIRST YEAR STUDENTS"

00:21:30.330 --> 00:21:32.540
The Rookie Events are starting today!

00:21:32.540 --> 00:21:34.500
Let's do our best!

00:21:34.500 --> 00:21:35.420
Yeah.

00:21:35.420 --> 00:21:39.380
Miyuki, I'm sure it's a lot to handle,
competing in Ms. Watanabe's place

00:21:39.380 --> 00:21:41.050
along with your Rookie Event.

00:21:41.050 --> 00:21:42.380
I suppose so.

00:21:42.380 --> 00:21:43.840
But I'll be fine!

00:21:43.840 --> 00:21:46.800
After all, I have my brother on my side!

00:21:46.800 --> 00:21:50.260
R-Right, you sure do, Miyuki.

00:21:50.260 --> 00:21:51.310
My, my...

00:21:51.310 --> 00:21:52.850
The same goes for you, remember?

00:21:52.850 --> 00:21:53.680
--Huh?
--Huh?

00:21:53.680 --> 00:21:58.940
Advising you on strategy, your training...
Who was always by your side?

00:22:00.190 --> 00:22:01.440
Yeah.

00:22:01.440 --> 00:22:02.570
You're right.

00:22:04.690 --> 00:22:06.280
The three of us...

00:22:06.280 --> 00:22:08.410
are going to fight
to the best of our abilities!

00:22:08.410 --> 00:22:11.580
Please watch over us, Brother!
